Box spacing shortcuts: {p: 6, mt: 5}. ✓ per traps file `spacing={{p: 4, mb: 3}}`.

Text color="secondary" — check valid: uikit Text color prop: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'complementary' | 'hint' | 'info' | ... yes 'secondary' exists.

Text variant="subheader-2" ✓, "body-2" ✓, "header-1" ✓.

Button view="outlined" ✓. Icon data={...} ✓.

Card view="raised" type container default ✓ size="l" ✓.

YagrTheme: CpuLoadChart props theme: YagrTheme — RealTheme = StringWithSuggest<'light'|'light-hc'|'dark'|'dark-hc'> → assignable to YagrTheme? StringWithSuggest is likely `T | (string & {})` — NOT assignable to 'light'|'dark'|... So `theme={theme}` where theme: RealTheme → type error passing to YagrTheme. Options: type state as 'light' | 'dark' (assignable to both RealTheme and YagrTheme). I'll use `useState<'light' | 'dark'>`. ThemeProvider accepts Theme ⊇ 'light'|'dark'. ✓ And CpuLoadChart prop type YagrTheme accepts it. ✓

Is `RealTheme` needed then? No — drop the import.

cpuData.ts — check numbers: WINDOW_SECONDS=86400 points ✓ "несколько десятков тысяч".

Also maybe add onSelect? Zoom is interactive already (drag to zoom, dblclick reset — uPlot default). Good enough.

Edge: `nextCpuValue` uses `new Date(tMs)` twice per call — called 86400 times at init; fine but slightly wasteful — compute once.

